        "root_concepts": "[grains]",
        "section": "food-plants",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Grains - The Grass Family Feeds the World",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TRIBE ORYZEAE (C3, tropical/subtropical)\n  └── Rice (Oryza sativa): 24 chromosomes (diploid); paddy flooded or upland\n        ssp. japonica (short grain, sticky) / ssp. indica (long grain, firm)\n        Staple for 3.5 billion people; primary calorie source in Asia"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-GRAINS.md#007",
      "path": [
        "01-GRAINS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
