        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Grains - The Grass Family Feeds the World",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TRIBE ANDROPOGONEAE (C4, tropical)\n  ├── Maize/corn (Zea mays): 20 chromosomes (diploid); highest yield/ha of any grain\n  │     C4 photosynthesis: more efficient at high temperature + light\n  │     Wild ancestor: teosinte (barely recognizable; <10 seeds per cob)\n  └── Sorghum (Sorghum bicolor): drought-tolerant; critical in Africa, India\n        Teff (Eragrostis tef): tiny seeds; Ethiopia staple; gluten-free"
    },
