        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "C3 vs C4 COMPARISON:\n  C3 (wheat, rice, barley): standard Calvin cycle; loses ~30% efficiency at high T\n  C4 (maize, sorghum, millet): CO₂ concentrating mechanism; higher efficiency >25°C\n  → Climate change (rising temperature) → shifts relative advantage toward C4 crops"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-GRAINS.md#011",
      "path": [
        "01-GRAINS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:food-plants:01-grains, git-history:food-plants:01-grains]",
